{"term":"deploy","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:8079b907da15a96be5","definition":"To prepare and arrange (originally military unit or units, i.e., to array troops) for use.","example":"\"Deploy two units of infantry along the enemy's flank,\" the general ordered.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["field"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"ergative","register":"ergative, transitive","wordFamily":["deployability","deployable","deployee","deployer","nondeployed","outdeploy","predeployed","undeploy","undeployed"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deploy#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:89de5af5e223e20362","definition":"To unfold, open, or otherwise become ready for use.","example":"He waited tensely for his parachute to deploy.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive, transitive","wordFamily":["deployability","deployable","deployee","deployer","nondeployed","outdeploy","predeployed","undeploy","undeployed"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deploy#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f88dd82e3e82cfb9df","definition":"To install, test and implement a computer system or application.","example":"The process for the deployment scenario includes: building a master installation of the operating system, creating its image and deploying the image onto a destination computer.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["deployability","deployable","deployee","deployer","nondeployed","outdeploy","predeployed","undeploy","undeployed"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deploy#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d6b85c06bf263e53ce","defin